  "repair_strategy": "Replace the ArrowRight (and ArrowLeft) cases in _onKeyChange with logic that increments/decrements the date by one day repeatedly until a non‑disabled date is found, using the same disability logic that the renderer employs (min/max dates, disableWeekends, disableDayFn). Leave ArrowUp/Down and other keys unchanged.",
  "edits": [
    {
      "path": "pikaday.js",
      "sha256": "a50b66482ec18884a7200882e9b523d9192b224b40b296cdd4080530f114fa75",
      "before": "        self._onKeyChange = function(e)
        {
            e = e || window.event;

            if (self.isVisible()) {

                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 1);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 1);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }
            }
        };",
      "after": "        self._onKeyChange = function(e)
        {
            e = e || window.event;

            if (self.isVisible()) {
                function isDateDisabled(d) {
                    if (opts.minDate && d < opts.minDate) return true;
                    if (opts.maxDate && d > opts.maxDate) return true;
                    if (opts.disableWeekends && isWeekend(d)) return true;
                    if (opts.disableDayFn && opts.disableDayFn(d)) return true;
                    return false;
                }

                switch(e.keyCode){
                    case 13:
                    case 27:
                        if (opts.field) {
                            opts.field.blur();
                        }
                        break;
                    case 37:
                        var current = self.getDate() || new Date();
                        var prev = new Date(current.getTime());
                        do {
                            prev.setDate(prev.getDate() - 1);
                        } while (isDateDisabled(prev));
                        self.setDate(prev);
                        break;
                    case 38:
                        self.adjustDate('subtract', 7);
                        break;
                    case 39:
                        var current = self.getDate() || new Date();
                        var next = new Date(current.getTime());
                        do {
                            next.setDate(next.getDate() + 1);
                        } while (isDateDisabled(next));
                        self.setDate(next);
                        break;
                    case 40:
                        self.adjustDate('add', 7);
                        break;
                    case 8:
                    case 46:
                        self.setDate(null);
                        break;
                }
            }
        };"
    }
  ],
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Keyboard users can now navigate to the next or previous selectable day using ArrowRight and ArrowLeft, skipping disabled days such as weekends. This restores logical focus order and improves usability for users who rely on keyboard navigation, satisfying WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) and 2.4.3 (Focus Order).",
  "functional_risks": [
    "If the minDate, maxDate, and disableDayFn collectively disable all dates in the calendar, the loop could become infinite (though this configuration is unrealistic).",
    "Performance impact is negligible for typical weekend skipping; however, navigating across many consecutive disabled days (e.g., a long blocked range) could take extra iterations.",
    "ArrowUp/Down (week jumps) remain unchanged and may land on disabled days; this is acceptable as the requirement only concerns day‑by‑day navigation.",
    "Changing the core navigation logic could affect edge cases near month or year boundaries where the disabled check interacts with min/max dates; these are mitigated by reusing the same disability logic used elsewhere."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
